<title>LATVIA: VEREINSBANK OFFICE OPENS FOR BUSINESS.</title>
<headline>VEREINSBANK OFFICE OPENS FOR BUSINESS.</headline>
<dateline>RIGA 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's Vereinsbank on Monday formally started operations at its new Latvia branch, in which the World Bank's International Finance Corp (IFC) also has a stake.</p>
<p>The branch is a subsiadiary of Vereinsbank's Vereins und Westbank unit and will carry out trade finance transactions and other general banking operations.</p>
<p>It joins Societe Generale as the only other Western bank in Riga.</p>
<p>-- Patrick Lannin, Riga newsroom, +371 721 5240</p>
